# OUSSAMA Cutter — Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` would otherwise copy the whole working tree
# into the image, including version control, tests, docs and — worst case —
# local secret files that happen to exist in the builder's tree.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored (the build needs them):
#   - requirements*.txt — the Dockerfile COPYs requirements.txt, and
#     setup.py lists requirements.txt, requirements-transcribe.txt,
#     requirements-transcribe-fallback.txt, requirements-upload.txt and
#     requirements-dubbing.txt as RUNTIME_ASSETS.
#   - .env.example — the documented template (cf. .gitignore's !.env.example).

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/

# Tests and documentation (not needed at runtime)
tests/
docs/

# Android app tree (Gradle). The container runs the Python WebUI only;
# nothing in the Dockerfile or the Python code imports from app/ —
# main_improved.py's `import app` resolves to webui/app.py (webui/ is
# inserted into sys.path first) and app/ has no __init__.py.
app/

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tmp-pytest/
.gradio/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Secrets and local credentials — never bake these into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
client_secrets.json
client_secrets*.json
token.json
yt_token.json
api_config.json
api_config.local.json
api_config.secure.json
*.pem
*.keystore
*.jks
local.properties
.viralcutter/
webui_settings.json

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Logs and runtime / output directories. The Dockerfile mkdirs VIRALS/
# and models/ itself and docker-compose mounts them from the host, so
# the image needs nothing from them; the rest are app-created outputs.
*.log
VIRALS/
models/
output/
tmp/
.polish_tmp/
final_polished/
updates/
